      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiang_Mai"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Chiang Mai’s name comes from the northern Thai words chiang, meaning 'city', and mai, meaning 'new'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chiang_Mai"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wat Chedi Luang, a large Lanna‑style chedi, was founded in 1401 and took many years to finish.",
